WEBVTT

00:24.360 --> 00:25.720
[gate squeaks]

01:13.440 --> 01:14.840
Service.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.400
[knocks on table]

01:17.920 --> 01:21.120
We do not open for two more hours.
You come back later.

01:22.080 --> 01:23.120
Police.

01:29.000 --> 01:31.000
Inspector Campbell, Sir.

01:31.960 --> 01:33.320
Any trouble, Sir?

01:34.480 --> 01:35.720
Look.

01:36.400 --> 01:37.600
I know.

01:38.960 --> 01:40.360
I know.

01:42.480 --> 01:46.080
That is, I am given to understand by
several of my officers...

01:46.840 --> 01:48.080
[clears throat]

01:48.160 --> 01:51.960
...several of my officers
that people come here.

01:54.000 --> 01:58.560
That men come here
for a certain purpose.

02:01.720 --> 02:03.600
[theme song playing]

02:13.080 --> 02:14.120
Arthur?

02:14.200 --> 02:15.360
Arthur, wake up.

02:16.640 --> 02:19.400
Get home, get bathed, check your kit,

02:19.480 --> 02:20.760
check your weapons.

02:23.440 --> 02:24.560
Why?

02:26.800 --> 02:28.320
What's going on?

02:30.160 --> 02:31.600
We're doing it today.

02:44.680 --> 02:46.360
Fetch the wagons, Charlie.

02:46.760 --> 02:47.960
It's today.

03:01.320 --> 03:02.720
[moaning]

03:09.640 --> 03:13.000
[boy] Dad? Our Katie's done
a wee in the bed again.

03:14.080 --> 03:15.960
I'll be there
in a minute, mate.

03:16.040 --> 03:17.160
[banging on door]

03:17.240 --> 03:18.280
[John exclaims]

03:18.880 --> 03:21.560
John? I told you
to keep the doors locked.

03:21.640 --> 03:24.400
I could've been anyone.
Now get dressed.

03:24.680 --> 03:25.920
We're doing it today.

03:26.000 --> 03:28.360
As a matter of fact,
he's doing me today.

03:28.440 --> 03:30.320
Make sure he's done you
by nine.

03:30.400 --> 03:33.840
- You should learn to knock!
- It's not a day for knocking.

03:35.080 --> 03:37.920
Dear Lord,
make this day pass well.

03:39.120 --> 03:40.880
Let none get hurt

03:40.960 --> 03:43.520
and make them that do,
not Shelby's.

03:45.080 --> 03:46.320
Watch John

03:47.200 --> 03:49.480
because he has so many
depending on him.

03:50.640 --> 03:51.840
Watch Arthur

03:52.840 --> 03:56.400
because he's likely to hurt
himself as much as anyone else.

03:57.360 --> 03:59.000
And watch Thomas.

04:00.640 --> 04:01.960
I know how he is.

04:02.920 --> 04:05.120
But he does what he does for us.

04:07.400 --> 04:08.600
I think.

04:09.680 --> 04:10.960
Amen.

04:17.480 --> 04:20.200
I used to do that every
morning during the war.

04:20.280 --> 04:22.520
I hoped I'd done it for the last time.

04:22.600 --> 04:24.600
Today will be the last time, Pol.

04:26.440 --> 04:29.560
After today there'll
be no need for prayers.

04:29.640 --> 04:31.040
We'll be set.

04:33.480 --> 04:35.520
Family meeting, half ten.

04:49.320 --> 04:51.200
I'm sorry I kept you.

04:51.280 --> 04:52.800
It is so early.

04:53.440 --> 04:54.840
Yes. I- I--

04:55.120 --> 04:57.600
I didn't sleep last night.

05:00.360 --> 05:03.920
Mr Zhang said you are
special, special customer.

05:15.840 --> 05:17.280
Do you want to sit?

05:25.880 --> 05:28.000
Do you want to take off your boots?

05:29.560 --> 05:30.920
Yes.

05:39.800 --> 05:41.800
And this.

05:47.520 --> 05:49.000
So tight.

06:01.920 --> 06:05.080
We can clean and press
your shirt while we do this.

06:05.840 --> 06:07.920
That's a very efficient service.

06:10.240 --> 06:12.920
You never been to a place
like this before?

06:15.120 --> 06:16.600
It's okay.

06:16.680 --> 06:20.120
Sometimes old men who have
lost their wives they come here.

06:20.200 --> 06:21.720
Most of the time.

06:22.280 --> 06:24.920
Old men? I am so old?

06:25.000 --> 06:26.160
[laughs] No.

06:26.240 --> 06:28.520
I mean I am young.

06:28.720 --> 06:29.880
Anyway...

06:31.760 --> 06:33.640
I'll make you young as well.

07:34.200 --> 07:35.520
Whore.

07:48.720 --> 07:50.680
[Campbell] Dear Grace.

07:51.240 --> 07:54.080
I write this letter to
you with a heavy heart.

07:54.760 --> 07:58.920
I know exactly what you did
and with whom.

07:59.800 --> 08:02.760
I will not mention any of it
in my report.

08:02.880 --> 08:07.120
However, you should be
aware that I know you gave

08:07.200 --> 08:10.440
yourself to the man who is
our sworn enemy.

08:10.880 --> 08:12.840
That is not only treason,

08:13.880 --> 08:16.920
it is disgusting
beyond all measure.

08:17.000 --> 08:19.320
Your father would be
ashamed of you.

08:20.080 --> 08:23.400
And as for myself,
I am beyond desolation.

08:23.840 --> 08:27.200
You have betrayed every
principle and standard

08:27.280 --> 08:29.960
of honor that was
your birthright.

08:30.960 --> 08:32.240
And for what?

08:32.480 --> 08:33.760
[Chin exclaims]

08:34.400 --> 08:35.800
Love.

08:38.640 --> 08:40.720
[Campbell breathing heavily]

08:57.920 --> 09:00.200
Oh my God. I'm sorry.
Did I do that?

09:00.400 --> 09:01.560
It's okay.

09:02.080 --> 09:04.400
You are special, special customer.

09:05.240 --> 09:07.280
Would you sit with me
for a moment?

09:07.720 --> 09:09.000
Please.

09:29.280 --> 09:33.400
[Mr Zhang and Chin
talking in Chinese]

09:43.080 --> 09:44.440
For the suits.

09:45.080 --> 09:47.120
You want to hear something funny?

10:11.000 --> 10:12.000
[gun cocking]

10:13.880 --> 10:15.360
I am unarmed.

10:20.080 --> 10:21.760
It's curious, Inspector.

10:22.320 --> 10:25.080
I thought you came here
to clean up the city.

10:25.160 --> 10:27.280
Not to sleep
with its whores.

10:29.400 --> 10:33.080
You're no different from any other copper
that came before you.

10:33.280 --> 10:37.440
I'm no different from those who would
follow should I choose to leave.

10:37.520 --> 10:39.160
You've no reason to stay.

10:39.760 --> 10:43.280
- You have what you came for.
- Yes, I have what I came for.

10:44.960 --> 10:48.120
I have a meeting
with Mr Winston Churchill at midday.

10:49.040 --> 10:53.280
I've no doubt he intends to congratulate
me on finding those stolen guns.

10:54.440 --> 10:57.880
And you still don't know how
we found them, do you?

10:59.320 --> 11:00.400
Good.

11:00.480 --> 11:02.040
No, you got lucky.

11:02.120 --> 11:03.160
Did I?

11:03.560 --> 11:04.480
Yeah.

11:05.680 --> 11:07.920
One thing I have learnt.

11:09.440 --> 11:12.160
Is that you and I are opposites

11:12.240 --> 11:14.320
but also just the same.

11:16.320 --> 11:18.040
Like an image in a mirror.

11:20.920 --> 11:23.360
We hate people.

11:25.000 --> 11:28.120
And they in turn hate us.

11:29.480 --> 11:31.240
And fear us.

11:35.440 --> 11:37.160
Before the day is over,

11:37.840 --> 11:39.880
your heart will be broken,

11:40.680 --> 11:42.280
just the same as mine.

11:46.280 --> 11:48.360
Men like us, Mr Shelby,

11:49.720 --> 11:51.480
will always be alone.

11:53.200 --> 11:54.720
And what love we get,

11:56.280 --> 11:58.040
we will have to pay for.

11:59.400 --> 12:02.040
You forget, Inspector.

12:03.480 --> 12:04.800
I have my family.

12:08.520 --> 12:10.040
Enjoy your day.

12:14.120 --> 12:15.400
[scoffs]

12:17.440 --> 12:19.000
[baby cooing]

12:22.240 --> 12:24.000
Oh, little one.

12:24.080 --> 12:26.360
You're much better
with him than I am.

12:28.040 --> 12:31.520
He settles quicker with me
because he can't smell the milk.

12:31.600 --> 12:32.800
You look tired.

12:32.880 --> 12:34.120
Let's put him down.

12:36.400 --> 12:38.240
[shushing]

12:39.560 --> 12:41.800
Mine were terrors for the tit.

12:42.480 --> 12:43.920
Both of them.

12:44.800 --> 12:47.200
Well, you never knew
my children, did you?

12:47.280 --> 12:49.040
I was a child myself then.

12:51.600 --> 12:53.200
You never talk about them.

12:54.120 --> 12:55.680
Never had reason to.

12:59.600 --> 13:02.240
My heart breaks even
when I think about them.

13:06.080 --> 13:07.200
But today-

13:08.320 --> 13:09.680
I do have reason to.

13:10.520 --> 13:11.920
Sit down, Ada.

13:21.200 --> 13:23.280
They were three and five years old.

13:25.200 --> 13:26.440
Sally was three.

13:26.520 --> 13:28.040
Michael was five. Well...

13:29.160 --> 13:31.160
Two weeks away from being six.

13:33.640 --> 13:35.000
It was Sunday morning.

13:35.360 --> 13:36.960
While I was at church.

13:40.680 --> 13:42.120
"You're not forgiven"

13:43.320 --> 13:47.880
this pinch-faced bitch said to me.
"You are not forgiven".

13:48.400 --> 13:51.320
You see, some sheets I washed
and hung on the line

13:51.400 --> 13:53.320
had the name of a hotel on them.

13:53.400 --> 13:55.320
They'd been stolen in a robbery.

13:55.400 --> 13:58.600
And they said some porter
at the hotel had been coshed.

13:59.200 --> 14:02.760
And a women from round here told
the police I had the sheets.

14:02.840 --> 14:04.960
Jealous, you see,
of the new sheets.

14:05.040 --> 14:06.920
And when the police came,

14:07.000 --> 14:08.960
they found a spirit still

14:10.000 --> 14:12.240
for making a few drops of Gin.

14:15.800 --> 14:17.120
And for that...

14:20.000 --> 14:22.360
They took my children from me.

14:24.800 --> 14:27.400
And they never told me
where they took them.

14:28.480 --> 14:31.680
And they did it because they could.
Because I was weak.

14:32.200 --> 14:34.920
But they'll never take
your baby away from you.

14:35.360 --> 14:36.680
Do you know why?

14:37.520 --> 14:39.360
Because Tommy
wouldn't let them.

14:39.920 --> 14:42.600
Because Tommy won't let them
walk all over us.

14:43.200 --> 14:47.120
Now it is Tommy that has brought
strength and power to this family.

14:48.200 --> 14:49.320
'Cause he knows...

14:50.400 --> 14:53.920
You have to be as bad as them
above in order want to survive.

14:55.960 --> 14:59.240
I'm telling you this because
I want you to forgive him.

14:59.320 --> 15:00.240
How can I?

15:00.680 --> 15:03.600
When my Freddie is rotting
in jail because of him.

15:04.200 --> 15:07.200
There's something about today
that you need to know.

15:14.840 --> 15:16.520
[keys jingling]

15:21.200 --> 15:23.320
Alright Freddie,
time to go.

15:23.400 --> 15:25.720
I want you to get
a message to Campbell.

15:26.040 --> 15:28.200
I can't let them
move me to Brixton.

15:29.880 --> 15:33.440
- If I get to Brixton they'll kill me.
- Freddie.

15:34.280 --> 15:37.080
You're not going to get
as far as Brixton prison.

15:38.720 --> 15:40.120
On your feet.

15:41.240 --> 15:44.120
I told the Prime Minister
personally that the guns

15:44.200 --> 15:46.720
had been retrieved
and he actually heard me

15:46.800 --> 15:50.200
and listened and I'm pretty sure
he gave me a half smile.

15:50.280 --> 15:53.600
He never usually smiles
unless a political opponent dies.

15:55.240 --> 15:59.040
I plan to put your name forward
in the New Year's Honors list.

16:00.680 --> 16:04.040
- That would be too much, Sir.
- Nonsense. You deserve it.

16:04.560 --> 16:07.360
As I recall, you wrote
to me several times

16:07.440 --> 16:09.720
about an undercover
operative. A woman.

16:12.240 --> 16:14.440
Was she involved in the discovery?

16:18.920 --> 16:21.520
Does she deserve some
kind of commendation?

16:28.280 --> 16:29.480
Yes.

16:30.040 --> 16:31.560
She was instrumental.

16:32.200 --> 16:34.880
A truly loyal servant
of the crown.

16:34.960 --> 16:37.320
And that is what
the record should state.

16:38.000 --> 16:40.800
And what of the men who
actually stole the guns?

16:40.880 --> 16:42.480
The Peaky--

16:42.760 --> 16:44.200
Blinders, Sir.

16:46.960 --> 16:48.520
If we were to make arrests

16:49.040 --> 16:52.120
the whole thing would end up
in open court and I know

16:52.200 --> 16:54.560
we wish to keep
this matter confidential.

16:54.640 --> 16:56.120
So they'll go free?

16:56.200 --> 16:57.440
Not quite, Sir.

16:58.960 --> 17:00.440
You see, I have plans

17:01.160 --> 17:02.600
for the Peaky Blinders.

17:06.560 --> 17:07.680
Alright.

17:13.360 --> 17:16.560
Right. I've got
you all here today

17:16.640 --> 17:19.920
because this is the day that
we replace Billy Kimber.

17:20.440 --> 17:22.920
This is the day
we become respectable.

17:23.000 --> 17:27.720
The day we join the official
National Association

17:28.040 --> 17:30.000
of Race Course Bookmakers.

17:31.640 --> 17:34.720
But first we do the dirty work.

17:35.080 --> 17:37.320
We've all known
this days been coming.

17:37.400 --> 17:39.560
I just haven't told
anybody the date.

17:42.320 --> 17:44.320
We're going to
the Worcester races.

17:44.400 --> 17:47.160
The track opens at one.
We'll get there at two.

17:47.240 --> 17:51.600
Now, Kimber thinks we're going there
to help him to fight the Lee brothers.

17:51.680 --> 17:54.080
But thanks to the efforts
of our John

17:54.160 --> 17:56.160
and his lovely new wife Esme,

17:56.240 --> 17:58.400
the Lees are now our kin.

17:59.000 --> 18:01.800
I interrupted those efforts
this morning and-

18:01.880 --> 18:03.760
but I can assure you all,

18:03.840 --> 18:07.080
John is making great sacrifices
for the cause of peace.

18:07.160 --> 18:08.760
Yeah. All right.

18:08.840 --> 18:12.840
So it'll be us and the Lees
against Kimber's boys.

18:13.360 --> 18:15.640
We take them out
but leave the bookies.

18:16.600 --> 18:20.800
I expect a swift victory which will send
a signal all the way to London,

18:20.880 --> 18:25.160
that we believe in letting legitimate
businesses run peacefully.

18:26.000 --> 18:29.200
And what about Kimber himself?

18:30.120 --> 18:31.800
I'll deal with Kimber.

18:32.240 --> 18:33.560
Any other questions?

18:35.280 --> 18:36.280
Yes.

18:39.160 --> 18:42.480
Does anybody object if I bring
a newcomer to the meeting?

18:46.600 --> 18:47.800
Come on.

18:50.440 --> 18:52.720
I'd like to introduce
the newest member

18:52.800 --> 18:54.400
of the Shelby clan.

19:04.480 --> 19:06.040
Welcome home, Ada.

19:07.520 --> 19:08.920
We named him Karl.

19:09.520 --> 19:11.000
After Karl Marx.

19:11.480 --> 19:12.680
Karl Bloody Marx.

19:12.760 --> 19:14.240
Let me get a look at him.

19:14.320 --> 19:15.600
Here we go.

19:15.680 --> 19:19.080
Hey, look. He looks just like me.

19:19.160 --> 19:21.720
That's his arse that
looks like you, Arthur.

19:21.800 --> 19:23.440
He's alright.

19:23.520 --> 19:24.840
He's a Shelby.

19:25.360 --> 19:26.880
Well. Ada?

19:28.240 --> 19:29.640
Am I forgiven?

19:30.240 --> 19:33.240
If what Aunt Polly says is true, you are.

19:35.480 --> 19:36.760
It's true.

19:39.560 --> 19:41.040
Thank you, Tommy.

19:45.480 --> 19:47.440
[Freddie] So who the hell
are you?

19:47.520 --> 19:50.160
[Michael] Someone who
wants to keep his eyes.

19:50.480 --> 19:52.360
They came to my house.

19:53.040 --> 19:55.000
Told me to volunteer for this.

19:55.400 --> 19:56.760
Who did?

19:57.520 --> 19:59.240
The Peaky Blinders.

20:06.240 --> 20:08.200
Tommy, Tommy, Tommy.

21:01.560 --> 21:03.000
Get out of the way.

21:05.600 --> 21:09.520
- What the bloody hell is that?
- Looks like your friends are here.

21:09.600 --> 21:11.760
[shells clattering]

21:13.760 --> 21:15.600
Stay down on the ground.

21:15.680 --> 21:17.240
Or the next one's for you.

21:22.240 --> 21:23.920
Make it look good.

21:24.000 --> 21:26.040
I am sorry about this comrade.

21:27.520 --> 21:32.000
- Holy shit! Danny, you're dead.
- Yeah. I've been living in London.

21:32.440 --> 21:34.920
Same thing. In you get.

21:35.000 --> 21:37.160
[all chattering]

21:42.200 --> 21:43.840
All right, lads, listen up.

21:43.920 --> 21:47.280
You have a pint and a chaser,
no more. On the house.

21:48.520 --> 21:51.160
Right. Let's get pouring.

21:52.200 --> 21:54.120
Do you have
the enclosure tickets

21:54.200 --> 21:56.800
and a register of book
keepers on the track?

21:56.880 --> 21:58.200
In me coat.

21:59.160 --> 22:00.720
You did a good job, Grace.

22:05.880 --> 22:07.360
The next family meeting,

22:07.720 --> 22:09.400
I'll make sure you're there.

22:10.480 --> 22:11.960
If I were family

22:12.040 --> 22:13.400
but I'm not.

22:14.760 --> 22:16.120
That could change.

22:17.280 --> 22:19.280
- Tommy?
- We'll talk about it more

22:19.360 --> 22:20.880
when I get back. Alright?

22:20.960 --> 22:24.560
- When will you be back?
- Now is this how you're going to be?

22:24.640 --> 22:28.360
You waiting at home for me saying,
"What time do you call this?"

22:29.920 --> 22:31.600
The barrel needs changing.

22:34.840 --> 22:39.040
Go on Tommy, go out the back and give
her a good seeing to before we go.

22:46.960 --> 22:48.120
Grace.

22:48.760 --> 22:50.920
Hey, Grace, I was joking.

22:52.080 --> 22:54.000
[John] Tommy, we need more mild.

22:54.080 --> 22:55.720
Just help yourselves.

22:58.200 --> 22:59.400
Tommy, the truth is

23:00.000 --> 23:02.840
when you get back from
the races I won't be here.

23:03.560 --> 23:05.160
What are you talking about?

23:07.240 --> 23:11.400
Alright, look. Grace, I know you weren't
born to be with a man like me.

23:13.600 --> 23:15.400
But I'm turning things around.

23:15.840 --> 23:17.560
When I get back here tonight,

23:18.280 --> 23:21.000
I will have one of the biggest

23:21.080 --> 23:24.560
legal racetrack syndicates
in the country.

23:26.280 --> 23:29.280
And I'm going to close down
some of the other stuff.

23:30.920 --> 23:34.080
Maybe open up a club, hey?

23:34.160 --> 23:35.680
Like in London.

23:36.760 --> 23:38.200
And another thing.

23:40.880 --> 23:42.920
You have a contract of employment.

23:43.360 --> 23:47.160
With a real Limited company,
you remember?

23:47.880 --> 23:49.800
I remember everything, Tommy.

23:49.880 --> 23:52.040
I am going to make
a success of this.

23:53.000 --> 23:55.760
I am going to make a success of it. I am.

23:55.840 --> 23:57.520
I know. I know.

23:59.360 --> 24:01.240
I'm not talking about marriage.

24:05.160 --> 24:06.640
We know each other.

24:06.920 --> 24:08.200
We can talk.

24:08.760 --> 24:10.200
We are the same.

24:10.720 --> 24:13.640
Tommy, I have done
something terrible to you.

24:16.560 --> 24:18.720
Right, tell him what
you just told me.

24:18.800 --> 24:22.160
Just heard there's two vans
driving up the Stratford Road.

24:22.240 --> 24:25.680
An old corporal of mine
said he recognized some of the men.

24:25.760 --> 24:29.000
He said it's Kimber's boys
and they're heading this way.

24:34.040 --> 24:37.200
Ada, wake up. You and the baby
get into the Bull Ring,

24:37.280 --> 24:38.960
where there's lots
of people.

24:39.040 --> 24:41.920
- What's going on?
- We've been fucking betrayed.

24:42.000 --> 24:45.120
Somebody let slip, Kimber's men
are on their way here.

24:45.200 --> 24:48.000
- But you can handle them Tommy?
- It's just us.

24:48.080 --> 24:51.040
All the Lees are all on their way
to the Worcester.

24:51.120 --> 24:52.560
We're outnumbered. Fuck!

24:52.640 --> 24:56.000
Who else knew today was the day
you were moving on Kimber?

24:56.080 --> 24:59.040
You said you kept it secret.
Who else did you tell?

25:00.480 --> 25:04.560
There's only one thing could blind
a man as smart as you Tommy. Love.

25:04.960 --> 25:06.360
It was that barmaid.

25:09.200 --> 25:10.560
I will deal with Grace.

25:11.600 --> 25:14.480
If you set eyes on her again,
you might kill her.

25:31.600 --> 25:32.840
Going for good?

25:32.920 --> 25:34.360
I heard there's trouble.

25:34.440 --> 25:36.560
Instinct is a funny thing.

25:37.200 --> 25:40.680
See, normally I can tell about
a person. But with you--

25:40.760 --> 25:42.880
Look, the fighting is
about to begin.

25:42.960 --> 25:45.920
- We should get out of here.
- We know who you are.

25:48.640 --> 25:49.960
Tommy knows as well.

25:50.040 --> 25:53.240
Turns out that copper as good
as told him this morning.

25:53.320 --> 25:55.800
But I wanted to hear it
from your lips.

26:01.440 --> 26:03.280
I am an agent of the crown.

26:03.360 --> 26:06.560
I have the power to arrest
and the right to use force.

26:06.640 --> 26:09.680
So please step out of my way.

26:09.760 --> 26:12.000
Like I say, instinct is a funny thing.

26:12.080 --> 26:14.440
You fell for Tommy
for real, didn't you?

26:15.240 --> 26:16.840
This gun is loaded.

26:17.200 --> 26:18.640
I'm not afraid of you.

26:19.360 --> 26:20.880
I feel sorry for you.

26:22.000 --> 26:23.400
Slip of a thing.

26:23.480 --> 26:26.520
You thought you'd come in
here and stitch us all up.

26:26.600 --> 26:29.600
We've had some coppers narks
in here before but you?

26:29.680 --> 26:31.360
You're the Queen
of them all.

26:33.480 --> 26:34.880
So who are you?

26:36.600 --> 26:38.400
A little rich girl, I'd guess?

26:39.200 --> 26:40.680
Unionist?

26:41.080 --> 26:42.920
An Ulster Volunteer?

26:44.040 --> 26:46.160
You thought Fenians,

26:46.240 --> 26:48.120
communists,

26:48.200 --> 26:49.680
low people,

26:50.200 --> 26:52.000
they're all the same.

26:52.400 --> 26:53.640
Scum.

26:54.400 --> 26:55.960
Then you met Tommy.

27:01.040 --> 27:04.760
I'd fight you with my fists
and show you how a rich girl fights.

27:04.840 --> 27:06.520
I'm from a tough family too.

27:14.000 --> 27:15.280
No.

27:17.360 --> 27:19.240
We women have more sense.

27:20.760 --> 27:22.840
Why don't you pour us both a drink?

27:35.520 --> 27:36.760
So am I right?

27:40.960 --> 27:42.440
Did you fall for Tommy?

27:51.320 --> 27:52.360
Yes.

27:52.680 --> 27:53.960
Then I pity you.

27:55.120 --> 27:56.840
I think he'll try to kill me.

27:57.840 --> 27:59.040
He's too soft.

27:59.120 --> 28:02.600
- Soft?
- Soft like you.

28:03.360 --> 28:06.080
You saved his life the night
the coppers came.

28:06.800 --> 28:09.280
That's why we're drinking
and not fighting.

28:10.320 --> 28:11.600
We owe you.

28:17.800 --> 28:21.560
What was he like, before France?

28:23.040 --> 28:26.000
He laughed, a lot.

28:27.640 --> 28:29.480
He wanted to work with horses.

28:31.960 --> 28:33.120
He won medals.

28:33.200 --> 28:34.520
Threw them in the Cut.

28:35.920 --> 28:38.280
Not a single man
came back the same.

28:40.560 --> 28:43.520
You know, after all this is over,

28:45.240 --> 28:46.760
he might forgive you.

28:46.840 --> 28:49.760
He might take you in.
You can never tell with men.

28:49.840 --> 28:54.360
They go for whoever their dicks point at
and there's no changing their minds.

28:54.440 --> 28:56.360
But I should tell you something.

28:57.600 --> 28:59.160
I will never forgive you,.

29:00.600 --> 29:02.080
Or accept you.

29:03.160 --> 29:04.520
Or take you in.

29:05.960 --> 29:09.320
And it's me who runs business
of the heart in this family.

29:10.640 --> 29:12.680
And as far as I'm concerned,

29:13.200 --> 29:15.120
you're a snitch from the Parish.

29:16.160 --> 29:19.080
And if you're not gone
from this city by tomorrow,

29:20.080 --> 29:21.440
I'll kill you myself.

29:27.560 --> 29:28.560
Now go.

29:43.120 --> 29:45.000
Maybe what really upsets you,

29:45.560 --> 29:48.280
is the thought that
one day you might lose him.

29:58.920 --> 30:01.600
Tommy. We've had word
from Nipper at Hay Mills

30:01.680 --> 30:04.480
and he says the police are
letting them through.

30:04.560 --> 30:07.160
And how come all our police
have disappeared?

30:07.240 --> 30:10.600
Because it was the police who
told Kimber about the plan.

30:10.680 --> 30:13.480
- And who told the police?
- You know what John?

30:13.560 --> 30:17.120
For all I think I'm the smartest one,
I'm guessing it was me.

30:20.040 --> 30:21.440
All right, men.

30:21.520 --> 30:24.160
You were mostly in the war so you know

30:24.240 --> 30:28.280
battle plans always change
and get fucked up.

30:28.360 --> 30:29.920
Well here it is.

30:30.000 --> 30:31.400
Things have changed.

30:31.480 --> 30:34.240
We fight them here. Today. Alone.

30:34.320 --> 30:36.360
Now they're gonna come
for the pub.

30:36.440 --> 30:38.960
They're gonna try
and break us up for good.

30:39.040 --> 30:41.480
And we'll have no help
from the law today.

30:42.760 --> 30:44.960
That pub there is
called the Garrison.

30:45.160 --> 30:46.920
Well now it really is one.

30:47.000 --> 30:49.240
And it belongs to us, right?

30:49.320 --> 30:50.520
[all] Right!

30:50.680 --> 30:53.760
- How many are there?
- Jeremiah says two Riley vans.

30:53.840 --> 30:56.760
So I reckon we're outnumbered
three to one.

30:56.880 --> 30:57.960
[Arthur] Fuck.

30:58.040 --> 31:00.680
But it's us boys. It's us.

31:00.760 --> 31:04.800
The Small Heath Rifles.
We never lost a fight yet, did we?

31:04.880 --> 31:07.480
- [all] No!
- Alright. Jeremiah.

31:07.560 --> 31:11.040
I know you vowed to God
you'd never pick up a weapon again.

31:11.120 --> 31:13.120
But can you ask him from me

31:13.200 --> 31:14.880
if you can help us today?

31:15.280 --> 31:17.880
God says he don't deal
with Small Heath, sir.

31:17.960 --> 31:20.120
[Thomas] Good man.
Arthur, Scud-boat.

31:20.200 --> 31:21.600
You'll take the flanks.

31:21.680 --> 31:23.600
- Just like at St. Marie.
- Sure.

31:23.680 --> 31:26.080
Curly, when a Shelby man
dies here today,

31:26.160 --> 31:28.000
you bury us side by side.

31:28.760 --> 31:31.240
All right. We have about ten minutes.

31:31.640 --> 31:33.440
Make your peace with whoever.

31:36.760 --> 31:41.400
We've had reports of a large group of men
in vehicles heading towards the city.

31:41.480 --> 31:44.040
Most of them are known
to the police, sir.

31:44.760 --> 31:47.440
We think a gang fight's
about to break out.

31:47.520 --> 31:52.160
I want all officers and constables
stood down in the following areas.

31:52.560 --> 31:54.800
Bordesley, Small Heath,

31:54.880 --> 31:57.480
Shard End, Greet and Hay Mills.

31:57.560 --> 31:59.560
- Stood down Sir?
- Immediately.

31:59.640 --> 32:03.160
And the vehicles approaching
the city should not be impeded.

32:03.240 --> 32:05.960
- What the hell is going on?
- Let dog eat dog.

32:07.520 --> 32:09.880
Let the beasts devour each other.

32:11.240 --> 32:13.800
And then we shall pick the bones.

32:28.120 --> 32:29.480
She's gone then?

32:36.560 --> 32:40.440
You're not accustomed to not getting
what you want, are you Tommy?

32:42.760 --> 32:44.960
You wanted my pub and you took it.

32:55.240 --> 32:56.800
You got a fair price.

33:00.400 --> 33:02.840
What I got was an ultimatum.

33:03.480 --> 33:05.240
Like you give to everybody.

33:05.320 --> 33:07.040
Do it or else.

33:08.240 --> 33:10.320
And yet it's funny.

33:11.120 --> 33:12.840
Everybody round here...

33:12.920 --> 33:15.080
They want you
to win this battle.

33:17.560 --> 33:19.000
I think what it is,

33:19.320 --> 33:22.640
you're bad men
but you're our bad men.

33:26.920 --> 33:28.680
Will you go looking for her?

33:32.800 --> 33:34.320
She is in the past.

33:37.840 --> 33:39.880
And the past is not my concern.

33:43.520 --> 33:46.200
And the future is no longer
my concern either.

33:46.280 --> 33:47.880
What is your concern Tommy?

33:50.400 --> 33:51.640
The one minute.

33:55.280 --> 33:56.840
The soldier's minute.

33:58.920 --> 34:00.800
In a battle that's all you get.

34:03.720 --> 34:05.800
One minute of everything at once.

34:10.280 --> 34:12.280
And anything before is nothing.

34:14.880 --> 34:18.120
Everything after, nothing.

34:20.920 --> 34:22.520
Nothing in comparison

34:23.400 --> 34:24.960
to that one minute.

34:31.000 --> 34:33.880
[Harry] Didn't you get enough
minutes over there? 

34:34.200 --> 34:35.200
[scoffs]

34:39.760 --> 34:41.240
It seems not, doesn't it?

34:43.200 --> 34:44.880
[door opens]

34:44.960 --> 34:46.760
[panting] Tommy, they're here.

35:31.760 --> 35:34.320
Get your weapons out boys,
and load them up.

35:38.800 --> 35:40.320
Take your time.

35:41.160 --> 35:44.560
Hold them up in the air so
as they can see what we've got.

35:52.160 --> 35:55.800
All guns and no balls, right, Billy boy?

36:04.640 --> 36:06.600
So what do we do now?

36:06.680 --> 36:08.320
Just give the order.

36:31.280 --> 36:35.000
The men who have arrived
in Garrison Lane are armed with rifles.

36:36.760 --> 36:38.080
Did you hear me?

36:38.640 --> 36:41.960
Their methods of self-destruction
are not my concern.

36:42.440 --> 36:46.320
We have also had a report
of machine gun fire in Saltleigh.

36:46.600 --> 36:49.320
The ravings of an old soldier
with shell shock.

36:49.400 --> 36:52.760
We only found twenty-four of those
twenty-five Lewis guns.

36:52.840 --> 36:55.000
If they were to get to use the one--

36:58.640 --> 37:00.000
You know when-

37:01.120 --> 37:04.080
when you came here from
Belfast I was overjoyed.

37:04.920 --> 37:08.520
I was sick of this force
and I was sick of all the corruption.

37:08.600 --> 37:11.800
When you made that speech
about cleaning this place up,

37:11.960 --> 37:14.560
I gave a little cheer inside.

37:17.040 --> 37:20.240
You said it was the devil's work
to look the other way.

37:20.320 --> 37:23.400
I am not looking the other way,
Sergeant Moss.

37:23.480 --> 37:26.200
I am looking directly
at the events of the day.

37:26.800 --> 37:28.760
And I like what I see.

37:36.200 --> 37:38.560
It doesn't have to be
like this, Kimber.

37:39.080 --> 37:40.560
Too late for all that.

37:40.640 --> 37:43.840
You bit off more than you can chew,
you little toe rag.

37:43.920 --> 37:46.360
And now we're taking over this shit hole.

37:46.880 --> 37:48.800
Well... If we have to use guns,

37:49.840 --> 37:52.120
let's use proper guns.

37:57.960 --> 38:01.640
Sergeant Thorne
reporting for duty, Sir.

38:04.000 --> 38:06.840
You were saying something
about being out-gunned?

38:21.880 --> 38:23.120
[Ada] Move!

38:25.440 --> 38:27.840
[baby crying]
What are you doing?

38:27.920 --> 38:30.520
I believe you boys
call this 'no-man's land'.

38:30.600 --> 38:32.200
- Ada!
- Shut up and listen.

38:32.280 --> 38:34.840
- Have you lost your mind?
- I said shut up!

38:37.040 --> 38:38.920
Now most of you were in France.

38:39.560 --> 38:41.560
So you all know what happens next.

38:42.560 --> 38:44.640
I've got brothers
and a husband here

38:44.720 --> 38:47.240
but you've all got
somebody waiting for you.

38:47.320 --> 38:50.120
Now, I'm wearing black
in preparation.

38:52.240 --> 38:54.240
I want you to look at me.

38:57.120 --> 38:59.400
I want you all to look at me.

39:00.080 --> 39:02.000
Who'll be wearing black for you?

39:03.680 --> 39:05.040
Think about them.

39:05.920 --> 39:07.720
Think about them right now.

39:08.760 --> 39:10.480
And fight if you want to

39:11.120 --> 39:13.320
but that baby
ain't moving anywhere.

39:14.920 --> 39:16.400
And neither am I.

39:21.760 --> 39:23.000
She's right you know.

39:24.520 --> 39:26.520
Why should all you men die.

39:27.080 --> 39:29.800
It should just be them who caused it.
[screams]

39:36.120 --> 39:37.600
[Freddie] Don't shoot.

39:37.680 --> 39:40.240
You're all right son. You're all right.

39:40.320 --> 39:43.960
Ada, move away.
Don't shoot!

39:44.040 --> 39:46.480
[men shouting]

39:46.560 --> 39:48.640
Hold your guns up.

39:50.640 --> 39:51.920
Enough!

39:59.760 --> 40:02.840
Kimber and me fought
this battle one on one.

40:04.160 --> 40:05.280
It's over.

40:11.320 --> 40:12.920
Go home to your families.

40:44.000 --> 40:46.960
Scudboat, Curly. Pick him up.

41:07.520 --> 41:11.000
[door opens and closes]

41:18.120 --> 41:20.080
I want to ask you one question.

41:20.360 --> 41:21.600
Then I'll leave.

41:22.600 --> 41:24.480
Tommy knows who I am.

41:24.560 --> 41:26.200
What did you say to him?

41:27.560 --> 41:29.480
What did you say to him?

41:34.360 --> 41:35.760
I told him--

41:37.480 --> 41:40.640
that his heart would be broken
before the day was over.

41:43.200 --> 41:44.680
So it seems

41:46.040 --> 41:48.400
you've broken two hearts, Grace.

41:52.040 --> 41:53.440
As well as my own.

42:00.720 --> 42:01.840
[door closes]

42:03.760 --> 42:05.200
[screams]

42:06.560 --> 42:10.040
[Arthur] Take it Tommy!
Take it! Take it!

42:10.120 --> 42:11.560
Hold him still!

42:12.400 --> 42:14.640
Come on! Come on!

42:18.280 --> 42:20.400
There. I still have the knack.

42:23.680 --> 42:24.840
Have a drink.

42:29.160 --> 42:30.560
All right. Deep breath!

42:30.640 --> 42:32.000
[groans]

42:32.080 --> 42:33.920
That's it! It's done!

42:57.400 --> 42:59.440
Now we can bury him properly.

42:59.800 --> 43:01.880
In the grave we dug for him.

43:03.680 --> 43:04.600
Yeah.

43:05.480 --> 43:07.160
It's high on a hill.

43:07.240 --> 43:08.720
He'd like that.

43:17.200 --> 43:19.200
- To Danny Whizz-Bang.
- Danny.

43:19.280 --> 43:21.200
May we all die twice.

43:24.760 --> 43:26.280
To Danny Whizz-Bang.

43:29.640 --> 43:31.000
Danny Whizz-Bang.

43:48.800 --> 43:50.160
[sighs]

43:50.400 --> 43:51.880
Come on,

43:51.960 --> 43:54.040
the day is ours.
Let's celebrate.

44:17.840 --> 44:18.960
Well?

44:20.040 --> 44:21.280
Who won?

44:22.760 --> 44:26.040
A Mr William Kimber
has been found dead

44:26.120 --> 44:27.720
with a gun shot wound.

44:28.320 --> 44:32.520
So I'm guessing that means
the Peaky Blinders won.

44:32.760 --> 44:33.760
Sir.

44:36.080 --> 44:39.640
Also the Communist agitator
Freddie Thorne

44:39.720 --> 44:42.920
was taken from his transport
by armed men.

44:44.480 --> 44:48.960
Since there were no officers on the street
at the time following your orders,

44:49.040 --> 44:51.800
he managed to escape easily
and is now at large.

44:53.040 --> 44:55.960
The prison officers said
they recognized the men.

44:56.040 --> 44:58.760
They were Peaky Blinders
as well, Sir.

45:00.480 --> 45:03.520
I mean we could go down there
and make a few arrests

45:03.600 --> 45:05.640
but no one will have
seen anything.

45:06.080 --> 45:08.920
And there were no officers
there to witness, Sir.

45:10.760 --> 45:13.160
The Shelbys will get
away with murder.

45:14.000 --> 45:15.720
Just like they always have.

45:17.360 --> 45:20.800
Some things never
change, eh sir?

45:27.880 --> 45:28.880
[door closes]

45:29.680 --> 45:31.760
[people cheering]

45:45.960 --> 45:48.960
[John] A toast...
A toast, a toast!

45:49.040 --> 45:51.040
To Shelby Limited!

45:51.120 --> 45:52.760
[people cheering]

45:57.720 --> 45:59.040
[Curly] He's got sons.

45:59.120 --> 46:00.840
Should we find work for them?

46:00.920 --> 46:02.680
No. Let them be.

46:03.160 --> 46:05.960
Let them find ordinary
work like ordinary men.

46:51.000 --> 46:53.760
Could you put me through
to Mr Churchill please?

46:55.840 --> 46:57.000
Yes, Sir.

46:58.040 --> 46:59.160
Sir,

47:00.160 --> 47:03.200
I've made a decision
about my future.

47:17.920 --> 47:19.520
Everyone's leaving town.

47:21.040 --> 47:22.960
- Tommy, you're hurt.
- I'm fine.

47:25.680 --> 47:27.240
What exactly can I say?

47:27.320 --> 47:28.520
I don't know, Grace.

47:31.400 --> 47:33.320
I could tell you who
I really am.

47:33.760 --> 47:35.400
I think I know who you are.

47:37.080 --> 47:38.400
And you know who I am.

47:38.480 --> 47:40.520
The circumstance is not important.

47:41.720 --> 47:42.960
Circumstance?

47:43.040 --> 47:44.280
Is all it is.

47:46.080 --> 47:47.400
Just uniform.

47:48.560 --> 47:49.800
Yeah.

47:55.000 --> 47:57.520
Some day I will throw
this gun in the canal.

47:58.400 --> 47:59.960
Why not now?

48:10.280 --> 48:11.800
Here it comes, Tommy.

48:14.720 --> 48:16.080
I love you.

48:18.760 --> 48:20.840
And there it goes, Grace.

48:22.800 --> 48:24.400
Away it goes.

48:25.920 --> 48:28.200
We can say it as much as we like--

48:30.560 --> 48:32.560
but there is no chance.

48:45.520 --> 48:48.440
I'll be in London one week.
At this address.

48:49.080 --> 48:51.440
Finish your business here and join me.

48:53.800 --> 48:55.440
I have an idea.

49:08.640 --> 49:09.840
[door opens]

49:13.080 --> 49:14.680
[Arthur] There he is...

49:14.760 --> 49:15.880
Drink?

49:20.960 --> 49:22.480
Not whiskey.

49:25.480 --> 49:27.120
If you check behind the bar,

49:29.400 --> 49:31.920
you will find a bottle
of Champagne.

49:41.880 --> 49:43.440
The one she bought.

49:50.400 --> 49:51.960
Today was a good day.

49:56.200 --> 49:58.360
All of Kimber's men
were busy here,

49:59.120 --> 50:02.720
so the Lee boys took all their pitches
at the Worcester races.

50:05.600 --> 50:08.400
It couldn't have gone better
if we'd planned it.

50:08.480 --> 50:12.120
Shelby Brothers Limited
are now the third

50:12.320 --> 50:16.600
largest legal race track
operation in the country.

50:16.680 --> 50:17.840
[drunkenly] Cheers.

50:17.920 --> 50:21.360
Only the Sabinis and the Solomons
are bigger than us, boys.

50:25.440 --> 50:28.000
And all my family is here to celebrate.

50:29.760 --> 50:31.000
[cork pops]

50:32.440 --> 50:34.320
To Shelby Brother's Limited.

50:34.960 --> 50:36.440
[Arthur] Shelby!

50:36.520 --> 50:37.600
Cheers.

50:54.320 --> 50:55.680
There'll be others.

51:04.440 --> 51:05.760
To the others.

51:08.000 --> 51:09.160
All of them.

51:41.360 --> 51:43.120
Dear Grace.

51:43.200 --> 51:45.960
Without a secretary
I write my own letters

51:46.320 --> 51:48.120
and I write without malice.

51:49.520 --> 51:51.720
I learnt long ago
to hate my enemies.

51:52.840 --> 51:54.800
But I've never loved one before.

52:00.000 --> 52:02.160
The idea of New York
is interesting

52:03.040 --> 52:05.400
but I have worked so hard
for this day.

52:05.480 --> 52:07.080
For this victory.

52:07.160 --> 52:09.120
I have responsibilities here.

52:10.160 --> 52:11.960
For people I need to protect

52:12.560 --> 52:14.200
and people who I love.

52:17.000 --> 52:20.320
Before the war, when I had
an important decision to make,

52:20.400 --> 52:21.960
I used to flip a coin.

52:22.560 --> 52:24.760
Perhaps that is what
I will do again.

52:27.520 --> 52:29.840
Polly tells me
you fell in love for real

52:29.920 --> 52:32.960
and Polly is never wrong
about matters of the heart.

52:36.320 --> 52:39.040
I will give you my decision
within three days.

52:42.160 --> 52:43.520
All my love.

52:43.600 --> 52:44.840
Thomas Shelby.

53:20.640 --> 53:21.840
[gunshot]
